    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99f6bf09_695fc7a9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawAtlas.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 686,
      "author": {
        "id": 13150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T15:37:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I moved it to the header. FWIW, here are my thoughts on this: Marking it \"inline\" here is probably a no-op on all modern compilers. Since all calls are from within this file, the compiler will inline it if it is likely to be profitable.\n\nI see two other differences:\n\n1. Code organization for humans\n2. Minor reduction of re-parse times for multiple includers.\n\nSince Plot is a private type and Plot::plotID() is the only function called from DrawAtlas.h, my preference would be to move more of the implementation to the cpp, now that I think about it.\n\nalways-inline seems like premature optimization and I\u0027d trust the compiler to judge whether it should be inlined.",
      "parentUuid": "66343115_f3e5bb1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 686,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 686,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "affa3e50158acbe72c8ee3f3113eac0566ae3ad5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
